{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"electronic-deducible-maggot","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\nTwo independent gaps make the live-Jira E2E tests' isolation story weaker than the code claims.\n\n### (a) `xdist_group` is inert under the distribution mode a local full-suite run actually uses\n\n`tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py:62-66` carries\n`pytest.mark.xdist_group(\"live_reconcile_e2e\")`, and the module docstring (lines ~57-61) states this\n\"pins every test in this module to a SINGLE pytest-xdist worker\".\n\nThat is true **only under `--dist loadgroup`**. Verified against the installed xdist 3.8.0:\n`xdist/scheduler/loadgroup.py:11-13` is the only scheduler that reads groups; `scheduler/load.py`\nand `scheduler/worksteal.py` contain zero occurrences of `group`/`xdist_group`, and\n`xdist/plugin.py:124` documents the mark as loadgroup-only.\n\nCI passes `--dist loadgroup` for the integration tier (`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:663`),\nso CI is fine. But `pyproject.toml:599` sets only `addopts = \"--strict-markers --strict-config\"` —\nno `-n`, no `--dist` — so a local `pytest -n auto` (exactly the \"full local xdist inventory\" that\nproduced the d30c regression report) gets xdist's **default `--dist load`, where the group mark is\nsilently ignored**. The protection the docstring promises does not exist locally.\n\n### (b) A second live-Jira test carries no group mark at all\n\n`tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli.py:155-172` — `test_reconcile_dry_run_against_live_jira` — runs a\nreal `rebar reconcile` dry-run against live Jira whenever `acli` is on PATH and `JIRA_PROJECT` is\nset. It has no `xdist_group` and no `pytestmark` (a repo-wide `xdist_group` grep returns only\n`test_reconcile_live_e2e.py:65` and `test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py:334,348`). It can therefore\nland on a different worker and issue a project-wide inbound JQL fetch concurrently with the\ndelete-permission probe's create+poll — under `loadgroup` **and** under `load`.\n\nNote also that `test_delete_permission_probe` is the only `@_requires_live` test inside its own\nmodule, so the intra-module grouping buys nothing on its own; the counterparty it needs to be\nserialised against lives in a different file.\n\n## Not the d30c root cause\n\nd30c's failure was fully explained and fixed without any load term (the poll's per-JQL memo made it\na single-shot check). This ticket is the separately-observed isolation gap, filed so it is not lost.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Either pin the distribution mode so `xdist_group` is honoured wherever the live tests can run\n  (e.g. set `--dist loadgroup` in `pyproject.toml` addopts), or correct the module docstring so it\n  no longer claims protection that only holds in CI.\n- [ ] Put `tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli.py::test_reconcile_dry_run_against_live_jira` in the\n  same xdist group as the live reconciler E2E module, so all live-Jira traffic serialises.\n- [ ] A test or guard that fails if a new live-Jira-touching test is added without the group mark.","id":"06f4-1c04-83c8-4a9f","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Live-Jira test isolation: xdist_group is ignored under the default --dist load, and a second live test is ungrouped"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787172547591392001,"uuid":"5db8dd41-e869-48a7-9071-468b766d6017"}